UnitEntrypoint::constructor
├── When access router is invalid
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_InvalidAccessRouter
└── When called
    ├── It sets the access router
    └── It should disable initializers on implementation

UnitEntrypoint::Initialize
├── Given already initialized
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
└── Given not initialized
    └── It should set the pool vault

UnitEntrypoint::Sweep
├── Given caller does not have ENTRYPOINT_MANAGER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with NotAuthorized
└── Given caller is entrypoint manager
    ├── When asset is native
    │   ├── Given recipient rejects ETH
    │   │   └── It should revert with SafeTransferLib.ETHTransferFailed
    │   └── Given recipient accepts ETH
    │       ├── It should transfer the native asset
    │       └── It should emit Swept event
    └── When asset is ERC20
        ├── It should query the token balance
        ├── It should transfer the ERC20 tokens
        └── It should emit Swept event

UnitEntrypoint::SetAssetConfiguration
├── Given caller does not have ENTRYPOINT_MANAGER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with NotAuthorized
└── Given caller is entrypoint manager
    ├── When vetting fee BPS is greater than or equal to MAX FEE BPS
    │   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_InvalidFeeBPS
    └── When vetting fee BPS is less than MAX FEE BPS
        ├── When enabling asset
        │   ├── When min amount is zero
        │   │   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_InvalidMinAmount
        │   └── When min amount is gt 0
        │       ├── When asset is native
        │       │   ├── It should set the asset configuration
        │       │   └── It should emit AssetConfigurationSet event
        │       └── When asset is ERC20
        │           ├── It should approve pool vault for ERC20 assets
        │           ├── It should set the asset configuration
        │           └── It should emit AssetConfigurationSet event
        └── When disabling asset
            ├── When asset is native
            │   ├── It should set the asset configuration
            │   └── It should emit AssetConfigurationSet event
            └── When asset is ERC20
                ├── It should revoke pool vault approval
                ├── It should set the asset configuration
                └── It should emit AssetConfigurationSet event

UnitEntrypoint::Deposit
├── Given asset is not enabled
│   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_AssetNotEnabled
├── Given value is below minimum
│   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_BelowMinAmount
└── Given asset is enabled and value is above minimum
    ├── When asset is native
    │   ├── Given msg value does not match amount plus fees
    │   │   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_InvalidETHAmount
    │   └── Given msg value matches amount plus fees
    │       ├── It should call pool vault deposit with correct value
    │       ├── It should emit Deposited event
    │       ├── When ciphertext is empty
    │       │   └── It should not call asp registry registerLabel
    │       └── When ciphertext is not empty
    │           ├── It should read the authoritative ASP registry from poolVault
    │           └── It should call asp registry registerLabel
    └── When asset is ERC20
        ├── When msg value is not zero
        │   └── It should revert with Entrypoint_UnexpectedETHAmount
        └── When msg value is zero
            ├── It should transfer tokens from caller
            ├── It should call pool vault deposit
            ├── It should emit Deposited event
            ├── When ciphertext is empty
            │   └── It should not call asp registry registerLabel
            └── When ciphertext is not empty
                ├── It should read the authoritative ASP registry from poolVault
                └── It should call asp registry registerLabel

UnitEntrypoint::UpgradeToAndCall
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    └── It should upgrade successfully

UnitEntrypoint::SetPoolVault
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── It should set the pool vault
    └── It should emit PoolVaultSet event
